Example 9: Simplify the expression \(4(x+y)-y\)
Using the distributive property, this expression can be simplified to
\[\begin{gathered}
4(x+y)-y=4 x+4 y-y \\
=4 x+4 y+-y \\
=4 x+(4-1) y \\
=4 x+3 y .
\end{gathered}\]

