3. For each set of lengths seen so far, you might have noticed that in at least two of the comparisons, the direct length was less than the sum of the other two (if not, check again!). For example, for the set of lengths \(10 \mathrm{~cm}, 15 \mathrm{~cm}\) and 30 cm , there are two comparisons where this happens:
![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/cfd9cba9-077b-4f37-a732-40ee0519eab8-267.jpg?height=269&width=210&top_left_y=997&top_left_x=1705)
\[\begin{aligned}
