If \(n\) is a number, then any multiple of \(n\) can be written as a positive integer multiplied by \(n\). For example, if we take \(n\) and \(5 n\) (short for \(5 \times n\) ), then \(5 n\) is a multiple of \(n\), and \(n\) is a factor of \(5 n\).

The HCF of \(n\) and \(5 n=n\).
For number pairs satisfying this property (i.e., one of the numbers is the HCF),
