\end{figure}

13 Hundreds \(\div 4 \rightarrow\) Each part gets 3 Hundreds, and 1 Hundred remains.
![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/cfd9cba9-077b-4f37-a732-40ee0519eab8-426.jpg?height=492&width=1362&top_left_y=1659&top_left_x=315)

Regroup 1 Hundred into 10 Tens.
10 Tens +2 Tens \(=12\) Tens.

12 Tens \(\div 4 \rightarrow\) Each part gets 3 Tens.
![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/cfd9cba9-077b-4f37-a732-40ee0519eab8-427.jpg?height=582&width=1434&top_left_y=345&top_left_x=315)

4 Ones \(\div 4 \rightarrow\) Each part gets 1 Ones.

