The average may not always be an appropriate representative of data that has outliers. A very high or a very low outlier can significantly impact the sum, thus affecting the average. For example, the 118 cm height in Poovizhi's family is an outlier at the lower end of the data. And the count of 40 short stories read is an outlier at the higher end of the data. In these cases, we saw that the median was not affected much by the outliers.

