\section*{A Mean Foot}

In the early 1500s in Europe, the basic unit of land measurement was the rod, defined as 16 feet long. At that time, a foot meant the length of a human foot! But foot sizes vary, so whose foot could they measure? To solve this, 16 adult males were asked to stand in a line, toe to heel, and the length of that line was considered the 16 -foot rod. After the rod was determined, it was split into 16 equal sections, each representing the measure of a single foot. In essence, this was the arithmetic mean of the 16 individual feet, even though the term 'mean' was not mentioned

